== Part 3. Reviewer's architecture: bytes moved per iteration ==
collect up = |V| x 12 B (x, y, mass as f32); tree down per consumer = cells x 24 B + |V| x 12 B, 0.72 cells per point
  |V|=1e+06: up 11.4 MiB; down per consumer 27.9 MiB; x8 workers 223.4 MiB; x64 tasks 1.7 GiB; fits one 128 MiB message: yes
  |V|=1e+07: up 114.4 MiB; down per consumer 279.2 MiB; x8 workers 2.2 GiB; x64 tasks 17.5 GiB; fits one 128 MiB message: no
  |V|=1e+08: up 1.1 GiB; down per consumer 2.7 GiB; x8 workers 21.8 GiB; x64 tasks 174.5 GiB; fits one 128 MiB message: no
  |V|=1e+09: up 11.2 GiB; down per consumer 27.3 GiB; x8 workers 218.2 GiB; x64 tasks 1745.2 GiB; fits one 128 MiB message: no
largest |V| whose full tree fits one 128 MiB message: 4.58e+06 (at 29.3 B per vertex); positions only (12 B): 1.12e+07
coarse grid at level L (dense upper bound 4^L cells x 24 B):
  L=6: 4,096 cells, 0.1 MiB
  L=8: 65,536 cells, 1.5 MiB
  L=10: 1,048,576 cells, 24.0 MiB
  L=11: 4,194,304 cells, 96.0 MiB

